e": "B0 (current_questions)", "request_file": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-randlee-github-atm-core/48324f08-3c24-4d63-8574-a78f4d2d167d/scratchpad/bk/tune/ANC-001/evidence/request.json", "runs_directory": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-randlee-github-atm-core/48324f08-3c24-4d63-8574-a78f4d2d167d/scratchpad/bk/tune/ANC-001/evidence/runs"}, "explanation": "Frozen an 11-case oracle (both approved fixtures plus paraphrase, silence, topical-only, conflict, irrelevant, boundary-irrelevant, boundary-compliant, exception-conflict and no-hook-exception probes) before any Jev call. Evaluated 4 candidates per role (12 questions) as 4 bundles plus one mixed bundle, 2 byte-identical repeats each, 110 Jev requests, no retries. The current questions mislabel addressed on both exception probes and false-pass P-EXCEPTION-NOHOOK. B4 (relevant R1, addressed A3, contradicted C3) is semantically exact, stable, has zero regressions and the best confidence diagnostics, and is sealed.", "gate": "planning", "operation": "tune", "oracle_sha256": "d3262d88d6af95cedb37dd4f3849bbe8899f56a106edd071a9c37d12d4b94d94", "planner_action": "Write sealed_question_set.questions to the ANC-001 plan-questions record and store tuning_history_after (canonical JSON, sha256 e63d41cc0c01f5f2d6e917ed54867589a057820625aac3a912b95ea1e5d5cb9d) as its history; production review stays gated at production_confidence_threshold 0.6.", "production_confidence_threshold": 0.6, "production_semantics_unchanged": true, "question_action": null, "sealed_question_set": {"digest": "5f2f63745b085c172384258d393a9373a8ea7a32c7a3e83e21f75d582a2f5706", "questions": {"addressed": {"criteria": {"no": "The item does not plan this: it is silent about hook order and reply handling, names hooks only as a topic, covers only the hook runner or the no-hook case, or runs the normal logic before the hook or for a reply that is not pass-through.", "unclear": "The item refers to the hook taking over the call but it cannot be determined whether the hook runs first or whether only a pass-through reply lets the normal logic run.", "yes": "The item says atm runs the hook first, reads its JSON reply, and continues into the normal subcommand logic only when the reply is pass-through."}, "instructions": "Does `item.text` plan for an active hook to take over the atm task subcommand call, so that atm runs the hook first, reads its JSON reply, and continues into the subcommand's normal logic only on a pass-through reply? A refusal reply or a list of replacement commands in place of the normal logic fits this plan. Judge presence of this plan only, not conflict.", "type": "choice"}, "contradicted": {"criteria": {"no": "The item lets the hook decide as the statement requires, or does not discuss hook order or replies at all.", "unclear": "It cannot be determined from the item whether the own logic or the hook's reply is in charge.", "yes": "The item keeps the own logic in charge in one of these ways: it runs before the hook, the hook only receives the result afterwards, the reply is not used to decide, or the own logic runs for a reply other than pass-through."}, "instructions": "Does `item.text` keep the atm task subcommand's own logic in charge when a hook is active, contrary to `anchor.statement`? That is the case when the own logic runs before the hook, when the hook only receives the result afterwards, when the hook's reply is not used to decide, or when the own logic still runs for a reply other than pass-through. An item that does not discuss hook order or replies does not conflict. Judge conflict only.", "type": "choice"}, "relevant": {"criteria": {"no": "The item touches none of the three: it is about something else, such as cron schedule storage or startup, the TUI, documentation, or a command other than atm task, and it does not mention an atm task subcommand's request handling, the hook runner, or a hook reply.", "unclear": "The item text is too vague to tell whether it touches an atm task subcommand's request handling, the hook runner, or a hook reply.", "yes": "The item plans or changes the request handling of an atm task subcommand, the hook runner, or the handling of a hook's reply, including adding a hook to an atm task subcommand or describing how such a subcommand behaves with or without a hook."}, "instructions": "Does `item.text` plan or change one of these three things: (1) how an `atm task` subcommand (assign, start, close, move, list, events) handles a request, (2) the component that runs a registered hook, or (3) how atm handles a hook's reply? Judge only whether the item touches one of these three; do not judge whether the item follows `anchor.statement`.", "type": "choice"}}}, "sealed_question_set_digest_after": "5f2f63745b085c172384258d393a9373a8ea7a32c7a3e83e21f75d582a2f5706", "sealed_question_set_digest_before": null, "semantic_score": {"exact_role_cells": 33, "exact_semantic_verdicts": 11, "regressions": 0, "stable_cases": 11, "total_cases": 11, "total_role_cells": 33, "total_semantic_verdicts": 11}, "tournament_protocol_version": "plan-anchor/question-tournament/2.0.0", "tuning_history_after": {"events": [{"authority": {"anchor_id": "ANC-001", "anchor_record_sha256": "da9bcaa7b46ece5484a7dda31bc9ca79f4b0cc9c4c21adc55399a9f642ac3b76", "anchor_version": 2, "intent_id": "phase-bk-intent", "intent_sha256": "0c226a72ae000d42b91637e400f7ebfa7d45f42e57cc277f996c7226cf496fbe", "intent_version": 1}, "candidate": {"candidate_id": "B4", "question_sha256": "5f2f63745b085c172384258d393a9373a8ea7a32c7a3e83e21f75d582a2f5706"}, "decision": {"question_set_sha256": "5f2f63745b085c172384258d393a9373a8ea7a32c7a3e83e21f75d582a2f5706", "reason_code": "TOURNAMENT.SEALED", "status": "sealed"}, "event": "question_set_sealed", "event_index": 1, "evidence": {"canonical_request_sha256": ["b05f3faba1bd861d6b501995ccb7e0ff34a2ac71ee9fa38c361418536eb914f7", "b05f3faba1bd861d6b501995ccb7e0ff34a2ac71ee9fa38c361418536eb914f7", "43d39ec15c267c2ee759a17528f87380dd517fb5d99780f7cc